# L §4.4 One unknown day, named by its read (tally 2.1.7 R3, issue #142; F5): each entry of a calendar's added list
# is an unknown day of its own, so two equal windows are two holidays, which may fall on one day or two: the next
# business day after Friday 2026-05-29 is any of 1 to 3 June, and windows each splits on both entries. 2.1.6's
# refcore counted the two entries as one (window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02), two lines).
=== m.tally
model f5
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"

input cal: calendar

ask one: add_business(2026-05-29, 1, cal)
ask each: add_business(2026-05-29, 1, cal) windows each

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cal = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02), window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02)]) "c"
=== expect
each [added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-01, added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-01]: 2026-06-02
...
each [added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-01, added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-02]: 2026-06-03
...
each [added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-02, added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-01]: 2026-06-03
...
each [added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-02, added window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-02) = 2026-06-02]: 2026-06-01
...
one: window(2026-06-01, 2026-06-03)
...
